+ *
+ * v402: scanout no longer waits for the first SwapEnd. v401 user space never
+ * reached a swap (backboardd starved before opening IOCoreSurfaceRoot), so
+ * no arm happened. n10_iomfb_publish() now also starts a thread call
+ * (THREAD_CALL_PRIORITY_KERNEL): 15 s after publish and then every 2 s (at
+ * most 43 ticks, last ~99 s after publish) it takes the single probe + arm
+ * (shared with the SwapEnd path, whichever comes first; probe tag "tmr").
+ * If that arm was refused only because the DPU/DECON state was not ready
+ * (why=probe, gc, trig or win: refusals taken before any mapping), the timer
+ * probes and arms again, at most 3 times, 5 s apart; every other refusal
+ * (chmap, format, geometry, iommu, iommu_mix, pt, page, map, order) is final.
+ * While no SwapEnd has been seen each tick sends one frame from
+ * the newest 1440x3040 4-byte IOSurface or, with none yet, from a 1440-pixel
+ * test row of eight vertical colour bars (white, yellow, cyan, green,
+ * magenta, red, blue, black; BGRA like the surfaces) repeated on every row.
+ * The frame takes the same path as a SwapEnd frame: armed state, one in
+ * flight, 100 ms rate limit, copy through the validated pages (0066), the
+ * 0065/0067 conversion and the two DECON0 trigger writes with the same
+ * checks. The first SwapEnd stops the timer frames. N402S at publish, N402T
+ * per tick (first four, every 8th, re-probes, last); N398F how=3 = test bars.
  */
